<title>CANADA: Planned Alberta pipeline ponders north extension.</title>
<headline>Planned Alberta pipeline ponders north extension.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Backers of a proposed natural gas pipeline in Alberta that would compete with the NOVA Corp system said on Monday they were evaluating a northern extension to the project.</p>
<p>The Alberta Pipeline Project group said it was mulling an addition north to the province's Kaybob region near Fox Creek, 300 km northwest of Edmonton.</p>
<p>The partners, which include ATCO Ltd unit ATCO Gas Pipelines, Shell Canada Ltd and Amoco Corp subsidiary Amoco Canada Petroleum Co Ltd, said the move was in response to strong interest from gas producers in the area.</p>
</text>
